  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council (nine divisions, two councillors each), polled 31 May 1911: contests in Camly, Lisleitrim, Lower Creggan and Newtownhamilton. Cullyhanna is not filed: three were nominated (James Donaghy, Patrick Green, Peter O'Hanlon) and there was no poll, but the withdrawal was not found. No party labels are printed. Polled 31 May 1911; counted at the Courthouse, Newtownhamilton (deputy returning officers Bernard Coyle and W. H. Starr). Two seats; the elected are printed in capitals and the old members marked with an asterisk. William Frazer and Patrick M'Geown, also nominated, withdrew. The Armagh Guardian's nomination list prints \"David M'Kenna, Tullyvallen\"."
